text:
lina: quick note from the console walkthrough 1: primary CTA in the compact toolbar is visually tight against the search field at small widths (seen at 360px). feels cramped and the icon+label rhythm is off. screenshot: https://img.redwood.example/console/toolbar-tight-360.png
omar: yep -- that area uses the compact spacing token. rather than widening that global token, i'd prefer a toolbar-scoped gap so other compact surfaces don't shift.
ben: Agreed. How about `--gap-toolbar-inline: 10px`? explicit name, tiny blast radius.
sasha: fine by me. Also spotted a focus/keyboard issue: when the toolbar CTA opens the run dialog, focus sometimes stays on the toolbar button instead of moving into the dialog on Safari VoiceOver. users can't reach the dialog actions with keyboard right away.
a11y-bot: accessibility finding: modal dialog missing reliable focus transfer on iOS Safari (heuristic failure).
lina: thanks. proposed CSS token and usage:```css
:root {
  --gap-toolbar-inline: 10px; /* used only for adjacent inline controls in toolbar */
}
.toolbar .action + .action {
  margin-left: var(--gap-toolbar-inline);
}
```
ben: nice and contained. for Storybook let's add a tiny viewport story at 360px showing icon+label buttons and the search to catch regressions. also add a visual snapshot so CI can detect reverts.
omar: modal focus suggestion: on open set `role=dialog`, `aria-modal=true`, and move focus to the primary control or a designated autofocus element. example:```js
function openRunDialog(dialog) {
  dialog.setAttribute('role', 'dialog');
  dialog.setAttribute('aria-modal', 'true');
  const target = dialog.querySelector('[data-autofocus]') || dialog.querySelector('button, [href], input');
  if (target) {
    // defer slightly to allow any transitions
    setTimeout(() => target.focus(), 0);
  }
}
```
sasha: that's helpful. also for toasts: we currently mark them with `role=region` and they don't always get announced. For error toasts let's use `role=alert` and make them focusable so keyboard users can retry. success toasts can keep `aria-live=polite`. sample:```html
<div class="toast toast--error" role="alert" tabindex="0">
  Pipeline failed to run. <button aria-label="Retry pipeline">Retry</button>
</div>
```
lina: one more minor copy thing: toolbar verb says "Trigger" while dialog primary button says "Execute". pick a single verb. I'm leaning toward "Trigger run" in the toolbar and dialog primary as "Trigger" as well for brevity.
ben: prefer a two-word label on the primary like "Trigger run" (clearer than just "Trigger"). agree to standardize. we'll keep CTA tokens for copy in tokens/copy.json.
omar: next steps summary: 1) add `--gap-toolbar-inline: 10px` token and CSS usage + Storybook 360px snapshot, 2) implement dialog focus transfer and aria attributes, 3) make error toasts `role=alert` + tabindex=0 and add an a11y Storybook story, 4) normalize copy to "Trigger run" in copy tokens, 5) CI snapshot + axe smoke for the new stories. i'll open a single PR for tokens + stories and a follow-up for the runtime modal/toast patches.
a11y-bot: queued a11y smoke test for new stories once PR is open.
sasha: thanks, folks. if someone can grab the PR reviews i'll check NVDA and VoiceOver after landing. :raised_hands:
